From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windowscodecs: info capabilities, TGA/TIFF decoding, block enumerators, query writers, DDS encoder (3500)

windowscodecs: component info capabilities, TGA right-to-left and resolution, planar TIFF, block enumerators, query writers, metadata content exports

The Decoder/Encoder/Converter/Metadata info objects answer GetSigningStatus, GetColorManagementVersion,
GetDeviceManufacturer/Models, DoesSupportAnimation/ChromaKey/Lossless/Multiframe (registry values, else the
built-in codec's known capabilities by container format), MatchesMimeType (case-insensitive over the
comma-separated list), converter GetPixelFormats and DoesRequireFixedSize.
TGA: right-to-left images are mirrored per row, frame resolution (pixel aspect ratio from the extension
area), decoder CopyPalette/GetMetadataQueryReader return the documented "none" errors, 32-bit premultiplied
colour maps are unpremultiplied, and the 24-bit colour map no longer ORs unshifted bytes.
TIFF: PLANARCONFIG_SEPARATE with 8 or 16 bit samples is woven into pixels.
IWICMetadataBlockReader::GetEnumerator for the common decoder frames, GIF and DDS (a shared IEnumUnknown).
IWICImagingFactory::CreateQueryWriter / CreateQueryWriterFromReader (a block writer of the factory's own).
WICMatchMetadataContent, WICGetMetadataContentSize, WICSerializeMetadataContent, and the
IEnumString_Next/Reset_WIC_Proxy exports.
DDS: the decoder's QueryCapability/GetResolution/CopyPalette/GetColorContexts/GetThumbnail/frame metadata
reader, and an encoder: BC1, BC2 and BC3 frames from 32bppBGRA pixels (WritePixels, WriteSource, Commit),
the file written by IWICBitmapEncoder::Commit with a DX10 header.
